A subset $U subset.eq V$ is a subspace precisely when it is non-empty and $lambda vb(v) + mu vb(u) in U$ for all $vb(u), vb(v) in U$ and scalars $lambda, mu$. In particular, $span{vb(v_1), ..., vb(v_r)}$ is always a subspace of $V$. The two trivial subspaces of any vector space are ${vb(0)}$ and $V$ itself.
